> Why two exceptional Sundays move back one week

h is a nominal lunar remainder. Treating it unconditionally as the offset to
the final corrected full moon misses exceptional ecclesiastical cases. It also
does not describe an observed lunar phase. A useful way to inspect the final
arithmetic is a fixed one-based March coordinate: March 1 is 1, March 31 is 31,
and April 1 is 32. Before the week correction, the nominal Easter coordinate is
22+h+l; the final coordinate is 22+h+l−7m.

Because 0≤a≤18, 0≤h≤29 and 0≤l≤6, the numerator of m is at most 469. It is
at least 451 exactly in these two cases:

\[
m=1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
l=6\ \text{and}\ \bigl(h=29\ \text{or}\ (h=28\ \text{and}\ a\ge11)\bigr).
\]
\alttext(The week correction is one exactly when l equals six and either h equals twenty-nine, or h equals twenty-eight with Metonic index at least eleven.)

For h≤27 the maximum is 18+11×27+22×6=447, too small. For l≤5 it is at most
18+11×29+22×5=447. Thus only h=28 or 29 with l=6 can trigger the correction;
substitution gives the condition on a. The quotient packages these cases in one
integer expression. In 1981 the uncorrected coordinate 57 would mean April 26;
subtracting seven yields April 19. In 1954, nominal April 25 becomes April 18.
The USNO specifically describes that year's ecclesiastical full moon on April 17.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/computus_exceptions.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(60,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.6;box.height=1.8;box.font_size=18;
  std::print("| year | a | h | l | m | uncorrected March coordinate | final March coordinate | Easter month/day |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  const std::array<int,3> years{1954,1981,2038};
  for(std::size_t row=0;row<years.size();++row) {
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::computus_gregorian_trace(years[row]);
    const double y=3-3.*row;const auto left=std::format("year{}",row),middle=std::format("nominal{}",row),right=std::format("final{}",row);
    box.fill={239,246,255};
    d.node(left,{0,y},std::format("Year {}\na = {}; h = {}; l = {}",t.year,t.a,t.h,t.l),box);
    box.fill=t.m?dm::graphics::RGB{255,237,213}:dm::graphics::RGB{239,246,255};
    d.node(middle,{6.5,y},std::format("Nominal coordinate {}\nm = {}",t.uncorrected_march_day,t.m),box);
    box.fill={220,252,231};
    d.node(right,{13,y},std::format("Easter {}/{}\nMarch coordinate {}",t.date.month,t.date.day,t.march_day),box)
     .edge(left,middle,"22+h+l").edge(middle,right,std::format("subtract {}",7*t.m));
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {}/{} |\n",t.year,t.a,t.h,t.l,t.m,t.uncorrected_march_day,t.march_day,t.date.month,t.date.day);
  }
  d.text({6.5,5.2},"Actual exceptional corrections, with a no-correction control",23)
   .text({6.5,-5},"Fixed axis: March 1 = 1; April 1 = 32",21)
   .save_svg("build/computus_exceptions.svg");
}
```
