> Domain, bounded work and integer limits

The single-year API accepts positive int years, including INT_MAX. Year zero
and negative/BCE numbering throw invalid_argument. Applying the Gregorian rule
before a jurisdiction adopted the calendar gives a proleptic projection; it
does not establish what that community observed historically. Other Easter
calendar conventions are outside this Gregorian calculation.

For positive int input, a≤18 and b≤INT_MAX/100. The largest expressions involving
b remain bounded by a small fraction of INT_MAX; the other remainders and final
encoding are small. The calculation therefore needs neither floating arithmetic
nor an unbounded integer. This is O(1) work in the supported fixed-width model,
rather than a statement that arbitrarily long integer inputs cost the same.

The summary checks both positive endpoints, their order and the complete inclusive
count before scanning. Its default positive cap is 100000 years. A complete
period requires the explicit larger cap shown above. It scans in ascending order
with O(N) work and constant 35-bin storage, and checks for the last year before
incrementing so that a range ending at INT_MAX cannot wrap. Returned data is owned;
there is no shared mutable state, input mutation or heap allocation in these APIs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::print("| supported positive rule year | computed month/day |\n| ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(const int year:{1,1583,2024,std::numeric_limits<int>::max()}) {
    const auto e=dm::algorithms::computus_gregorian(year);
    std::print("| {} | {}/{} |\n",year,e.month,e.day);
  }
  bool invalid=false,limited=false;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::computus_gregorian(0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::computus_gregorian_summary(2000,2040,40);}catch(const std::length_error&){limited=true;}
  const auto complete=dm::algorithms::computus_gregorian_summary(2000,2040,41);
  const int last=std::numeric_limits<int>::max();
  const auto edge=dm::algorithms::computus_gregorian_summary(last-1,last,2);
  if(!invalid || !limited || complete.year_count!=41 || edge.year_count!=2 || edge.last_year!=last)return 1;
  std::print("\nYear zero throws invalid_argument. A 40-year cap rejects the complete 41-year interval; cap 41 succeeds.\nA two-year range ending at INT_MAX terminates with {} years.\n",edge.year_count);
}
```
